course: dictionary
lesson: 14922
title: Refrigerated: kept cold to stay fresh
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Keep refrigerated» is written on many food labels. Refrigerated means kept cold, in a fridge or a cold room, so that food or medicine stays fresh. The clue is the word keep: you keep something cold so it stays good.
explain: «The milk must be refrigerated after it is opened.» The sentence tells you the milk needs a cold place, so refrigerated must mean kept in a fridge. Try your meaning in the sentence: «The milk must be kept in a fridge after it is opened.» It still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
explain: «The refrigerated lorry drove all night to the port.» A lorry is a big truck, and a refrigerated lorry has a cold box inside to carry food a long way. The verb refrigerate means to make something cold like this.
fact: Refrigerated means kept cold in a fridge or a cold room so that food or medicine stays fresh.
fact: Cold slows down germs, so food lasts longer when it is refrigerated.
fact: Milk, meat and some medicines must be refrigerated to stay safe.
fact: A refrigerated lorry or truck has a cold box to carry food a long way.
fact: Refrigerated is the past form of the verb refrigerate, which means to keep something cold.
exercise: «Keep refrigerated after opening.» What does refrigerated mean here? | Thrown away at once | *Kept cold in a fridge | Kept in a school bag | Left on a sunny windowsill
exercise: Which food must be refrigerated to stay safe? | Paper | Pencils | Sand | *Milk
exercise: «The refrigerated lorry drove all night.» Why does the lorry have a cold box? | *To carry food a long way without it going off | To make the lorry go faster | To keep the driver warm | To store sand and stones
test: What does a «refrigerated section» in a supermarket most likely mean? | A place for cleaning tools | A corner for sitting and resting | *A shelf of foods kept cold in fridges | A shelf of toys and games
test: Refrigerated is the past form of which verb? | Freeze | Heat | *Refrigerate | Warm
exam: «Medicine that is refrigerated stays fresh.» What does refrigerated mean? | *Kept cold so it stays fresh | Kept outside in the rain | Kept in a dark cupboard | Kept hot in an oven
